in @prism

in @epistemologic/silicon/arch/arm64
in @epistemologic/silicon/arch/x86_64
in @epistemologic/silicon/memory
in @epistemologic/silicon/flake_ref
in @epistemologic/silicon/compute_bound
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed
in @epistemologic/property/autopoietic
in @epistemologic/property/is_prism_record
in @epistemologic/property/frame_relativity

# @mirror/shard
#
# The observer-relative deployment description. A shard names what
# the observer CAN SEE from inside the system they are running:
# which silicon, which memory model, which flakes are reachable,
# which compute budget is rationed, and which parent shard (if any)
# this one nests inside. The shard is to mirror what flake.nix is
# to nix — the manifest that closes the world — with one structural
# difference: it is RELATIVISTIC. `self()` evaluated on bare metal
# returns the host's shard; the same expression evaluated inside a
# gen_prism returns the parent shard restricted to the spawn-time
# budget. Same source AST + different shards = different Au binaries.
#
# Per docs/specs/shard-design.md: five fields, one per Prism
# operation. Per docs/insights/2026-05-25-shard-as-observer-relative-
# lambda-zero.md: the shard IS λ₀ — the autopoietic closure of the
# deployment description; `parent: option(zoom(oid, shard))` is the
# Lawvere fixed-point witness; the chain terminates at bare metal
# (`parent: none`). Per docs/insights/2026-05-25-pipe-hole-and-au-
# binary.md: the shard IS Fate's tournament input — `binary = a |\>
# b` reads `@mirror/shard.self()` and picks the locally-optimal
# instruction subset, memory pattern, GPU backend. Per docs/insights/
# 2026-05-25-time-as-substrate-and-postgres-heritage.md: the parent
# chain IS the frame-conversion path; comparing two wall durations
# across shards walks to the nearest common ancestor.
#
# Substrate decisions (Alex 2026-05-25, prior tick):
#
#   Q1: spec coexists with shard. @mirror/spec describes what to
#       build; @mirror/shard describes where to run. The placeholder
#       at boot/std/mirror/spec.mirror is left alone.
#   Q2: Inheritance is INTERSECTION, LATERAL, ALWAYS. Children
#       narrow parents; siblings compose by intersection. No override.
#       The lattice property is non-negotiable.
#   Q3: self() re-resolves via the fragmentation cache. Same input
#       fingerprint -> same key -> cache hit. Hot-reload on hardware
#       change is structural.
#
# The four property declarations at the bottom are the math made
# load-bearing: content-addressed (identity = hash), autopoietic
# (the parent chain closes via Lawvere fixed point), is_prism_record
# (five fields, one per operation; drop one and the algebra rejects
# the record), frame_relativity (timestamps across shards require
# explicit conversion through the parent chain).
#
# Spec: docs/specs/shard-design.md
# Insights: docs/insights/2026-05-25-shard-as-observer-relative-lambda-zero.md,
#           docs/insights/2026-05-25-pipe-hole-and-au-binary.md,
#           docs/insights/2026-05-25-time-as-substrate-and-postgres-heritage.md

grammar @mirror/shard {

  # The shard record. Five fields. One per Prism operation. The
  # algebra closes at five; drop one and is_prism_record rejects
  # the type.
  #
  #   silicon  -> focus    : the manifold's hardware basis. The
  #                          arch carrier the observer is running on.
  #                          Sum over @epistemologic/silicon/arch/*
  #                          because no abstract `silicon` root
  #                          carrier has been declared yet (parked
  #                          design call from Mara's α work); the
  #                          sum directly addresses what exists.
  #   memory   -> project  : the available state space. Memory model
  #                          + budget + page size + cache hierarchy,
  #                          per @epistemologic/silicon/memory.
  #   flakes   -> split    : the composed nix flake stack. A list of
  #                          flake_refs, each locked to a rev so the
  #                          set is content-addressed-by-source.
  #   compute  -> zoom     : the budget envelope. All five bounds
  #                          (cores, host memory, GPU memory, wall
  #                          time, reductions) per @epistemologic/
  #                          silicon/compute_bound.
  #   parent   -> refract  : λ₀ fixed-point witness. option(zoom(oid,
  #                          shard)) — the OID of the enclosing
  #                          shard, or none at bare metal. The chain
  #                          IS the frame-conversion path; the
  #                          terminator IS λ₀.
  type shard = {
    silicon: arm64 | x86_64,
    memory:  memory,
    flakes:  [flake_ref],
    compute: compute_bound,
    parent:  option(zoom(oid, shard)),
  }

  # ── self: the observer-relative constructor ─────────────────────
  #
  # The relativistic constructor. Resolves against the running
  # observer's context. On bare metal: reads each silicon carrier's
  # detect() and the compute_bound.detect_max(), fills `flakes` from
  # `nix profile list`, sets `parent: none`. Inside a gen_prism:
  # reads the parent shard and applies the spawn-time restriction
  # overlay (intersection per Q2).
  #
  # Body is a Fate-resolved hole. Per Q3: re-resolution rides the
  # fragmentation cache; same input fingerprint -> same OID -> cache
  # hit. The observer IS the missing argument; Fate reads the runtime
  # context as the tournament input and produces the typed shard.
  self() -> shard { \ }

  # ── to_flake: shard -> content-addressed flake_ref ──────────────
  #
  # The load-bearing morphism. Compiles a shard into a flake
  # reference whose locked rev IS the content-address of the
  # produced derivation. Return is zoom(oid, flake_ref): a flake_ref
  # annotated with the OID that names this exact (shard, derivation)
  # pair. The OID cross-checks against @fragmentation.oid(s) per the
  # design doc §5 pipeline.
  #
  # Body is a Fate-resolved hole — the pipe-hole-and-au-binary.md
  # pattern. The tournament reads the shard, picks the instruction
  # subset, memory pattern, GPU backend, parallelism strategy that
  # maximize conductivity against the shard, and emits the flake
  # derivation. Same source AST + different shards = different Au
  # binaries, same verification chain.
  to_flake(s: shard) -> zoom(oid, flake_ref) { \ }

  # ── admits: structural bounds check ─────────────────────────────
  #
  # Does this shard admit the requested compute? The boundary
  # rejection per design §6: when a gen_prism asks to spawn, the
  # caller runs admits(host_shard, request); a fail diagnostic
  # names the violated bound ("child requests 32 GB; host budget is
  # 16 GB" / "child requires AVX-512; host silicon is arm64"). The
  # peer never starts running with infeasible resources.
  #
  # Returns imperfect so the failure path carries diagnostics
  # through the standard recovery surface — same shape as @io.read
  # and @time.convert. Body is a Fate-resolved hole; the tournament
  # picks the per-field comparison strategy against the carrier
  # types (intersection per Q2: every requested bound must fit
  # inside the corresponding shard bound; missing request fields
  # inherit the shard's value).
  admits(s: shard, request: compute_bound) -> imperfect { \ }

  # ── properties: the math made load-bearing ──────────────────────
  #
  # The four substrate-level claims the shard makes structurally:
  #
  #   content_addressed : identity IS the content hash. The shard's
  #                       OID determines its identity; two shards with
  #                       the same five-field content produce the same
  #                       OID. Foundational — the other three rest on
  #                       this one.
  #   autopoietic       : the parent chain closes via a Lawvere fixed
  #                       point. `parent: option(zoom(oid, shard))` is
  #                       a content-addressed self-reference; Banach
  #                       contraction on hash space guarantees the
  #                       fixed point exists and is unique. The chain
  #                       terminates at bare metal (parent: none) — λ₀.
  #   is_prism_record   : five fields, one per Prism operation. Drop
  #                       one and the type rejects. The contract is
  #                       declared here; structural enforcement lands
  #                       when the verifier wires up (parked Q from
  #                       the parametric-types tick).
  #   frame_relativity  : timestamps across shards are observer-
  #                       relative; cross-shard compare requires
  #                       @time.convert resolving through the parent
  #                       chain. Per PG §2.1 (timestamptz over
  #                       timestamp) at the substrate altitude.
  requires content_addressed(shard)
  requires autopoietic(shard)
  requires is_prism_record(shard)
  requires frame_relativity(shard)
}

out shard
out self
out to_flake
out admits
out @mirror/shard
